            <div xml:id="d396">

                <pb facs="0777" n="681" xml:id="pg681"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.6363/1900: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sheffield</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-07-23T12:00:00-07:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 23,
                                1926—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received 3:53 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>319. I now find that information transmitted in the last paragraph of Embassy’s
                    telegram number 317, July 19, 2 p.m. was incorrect. I was informed today that
                    all companies including Corona, Aguila, and Marland are firm in their opposition
                    to the order of June 8 if it remains unmodified.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sheffield</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
